{"arena": "Z", "t": 1792890949.8, "seq": 50, "op": "mutate", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "cost": 0.00054622, "parents": ["Z26"], "log": {"edges": [["progress", "goal_field", "call"], ["score", "progress", "call"]], "n_edges": 2, "editable": ["Z32b", "Z45a", "s3"], "llm": {"in": 863, "out": 819, "cache_read": 5042, "cache_write": 0, "seconds": 3.8, "stop": "end_turn"}, "reply": "This mutation makes `progress` more cautious when the bot is hurt. Enemy champions within attack range (3, not 2) now count, and each one's penalty grows as my health falls. `goal_field` and `score` are unchanged.\n\n```python\n@gene('Z32b', 'closer step toward goals, minus a penalty for enemy champions within attack range of the destination (heavier when I am hurt); unreachable tiles are rejected', parents=['Z32b', 's4'])\ndef progress(t: Tile) -> Num:\n    f = goal_field()\n    there = at(f, t)\n    if there >= 1000000000:\n        return -1\n    step = at(f, me().pos) - there\n    danger = count(1 for u in enemies() if u.is_champion and dist(u.pos, t) <= 3)\n    return step * 2 - danger * (3 + (1 - me().health_frac) * 6)\n```"}, "error": "GenomeError: progress line 63: expected Bool, got Num", "birth": 27, "accepted": false, "fingerprint": null}
